Package: Routbreak
Title: Outbreak Reproduction Ratios in Spatially Structured Populations
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Boxuan", "Wang", email = "wangboxuan990617@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Eugenio", "Valdano", role = "ctb")
  )
Description: Computes outbreak probabilities and outbreak reproduction ratios
    for multitype Poisson and independent-edge negative-binomial branching
    processes. The implementation follows
    Wang and Valdano (2026) <doi:10.1371/journal.pcbi.1014425>, using a
    reproduction matrix whose rows are infection destinations and whose
    columns are infection sources. It estimates reproduction matrices from
    generation-resolved transmission counts or sufficient statistics under a
    Gamma-Poisson model, and propagates posterior uncertainty to outbreak
    quantities. It also provides reference, local, and total reproduction
    ratios and constructs reproduction matrices from colocation data.
